{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350232-when-and-why-did-the-garou-get-their-tribes","id":1350232,"title":"When and why did the Garou get their tribes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-22T07:54:50-08:00","id":1350232,"title":"When and why did the Garou get their tribes?","content":"I bought Shattered Dreams a while ago, and it mentions that if you have a game in prehistory, the Garou don't have Tribes. When did they get them? How?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T11:53:53-08:00","id":1350277,"title":"","content":"There are different ideas and this period of history is difficult to gain concrete information on, particularly as one of the best resources Shattering Dreams is only considered quasi-canon.<br /> <br /> Anyway, preamble aside, I believe it's generally considered that the Garou were one tribe, one pack, following Wolf until around the end of the last Ice Age, when Death Wolf supposedly lent his secrets to some and the alphas of the Nation were blessed by Luna. This led to the rise of the Silver Fangs and White Howlers who were known to have the hides of Death Wolf.<br /> <br /> After this the tribes developed alongside the development of humanity and these dates are semi-headcanons co-opted from Black Fox but I do like them.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons emerged soon after humanity began domesticating animals, particularly Dogs, as protectors of the wild. The Black Furies, Fianna, Get of Fenris, Shadow Lords and Silent Striders arose from within their various host cultures; same as the Bunyip in Australia and the Wendigo, Croatan, and Uktena in the Americas.<br /> <br /> Furthermore we have the Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia, Glass Walkers, and Stargazers who likely joined together for a mix of ideological and practical reasons as humanity began to rise and after the War of Rage and Impergium.<br /> <br /> We all know where the Black Spiral Dancers come from...<br /> <br /> A notable tid bit of all of this is that it's suggested in a few places that the reason why Wolf is no longer a totem of the Garou is that after his children turned their backs on him and each other to follow tribal totems, he departed into the deep umbra to never be heard from again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T11:58:15-08:00","id":1350278,"title":"","content":"The Beforetimes, in the Long Long Ago ....<br /> <br /> How and why has always been somewhat nebulous. Personally, I've always suspected the how and why of the Impergium ending may have been tied into it. And I'm sure that the Silver Fangs claim that they were the first to convince a tribal totem of their worthiness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T13:04:59-08:00","id":1350292,"title":"","content":"According to the White Howler Tribebook, it was sometime during the last Ice Age. Shattered Dreams also says that the Garou Nation had already split into various tribes by the end of the Ice Age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T13:33:05-08:00","id":1350297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350232-when-and-why-did-the-garou-get-their-tribes?p=1350278#post1350278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm sure that the Silver Fangs claim that they were the first to convince a tribal totem of their worthiness.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Revised Tribebook, the stronger implication is that the Silver Fangs were one of the last of the ancient Tribes to form, because after the Tribes started to form, the Garou became to fractured and it was the proto-Silver Fangs that took on the quest to become the Tribe of Kings to reunify the Garou under their banner.<br /> <br /> Still rather self-serving and self-aggrandizing of course, but there's a certain sense to it rather than worrying about who was first as it focuses on why they're necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T15:08:48-08:00","id":1350320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350232-when-and-why-did-the-garou-get-their-tribes?p=1350292#post1350292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the White Howler Tribebook, it was sometime during the last Ice Age. Shattered Dreams also says that the Garou Nation had already split into various tribes by the end of the Ice Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, that's before the Impergium then. And I think before the War of Rage, but I'm not sure? (I mean, I guess most of the War of Rage was in places not covered by the great ice anyway, such as the Middle East against the Apis?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T17:44:15-08:00","id":1350353,"title":"","content":"My &quot;true history&quot; is that, by starting to deal with spirits for power over others, security and wealth the Garou and other Fera created awful imbalances as they completed spiritual chimage. This lead to the formation of spirit broods and werewolf tribes, unions of a sort. This is the Basis for basically everything wrong with the world of darkness besides, y'know, God and Mages.<br /> <br /> Of course, Garou are great talespinners and millenia has twisted this truth into variable narratives that change from tribe to tribe and elder to elder. Gryfon's pretty much there with what people believe. Maybe Garou were supposed to be devoted to wolf, but oh how they strayed for power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T17:45:21-08:00","id":1350355,"title":"","content":"I think in terms of prehistory, everything is supposed to be as vague as it needs to for things to be suitably mythic. Anything before @6000 BC in the WoD is pretty much an open canvas that can be whatever a gameline needs it to be. (And it's arguable that you may have had multiple realities happening at once, only to collapse in on itself at some point in the Bronze Age. This could possibly even include multiple realities in a single game line, resulting in conflicting myths and legends, or even memories in the case of the Mokole. The creationist nature of certain parts of Werewolf cosmology only add to it.)<br /> <br /> Regarding Wolf as a totem, for my own games I ended up borrowing some bits from Forsaken, in that there was a Father Wolf that was the original progenitor of the Garou, his part-material offspring the Hero Twins who were the first Homid and Lupus (yes, twins born to seperate mothers, because sometimes that's how gods roll; and the twins genders vary from story to story*), and his five totally spirit offspring that represent each Auspice. But while all off these are revered cultural icons-come-gods, none of them sponsor tribes or pacts. (I even stopped having tribal totems sponsor pacts for assorted reasons.)<br /> <br /> *Obviously most of the Black Fury versions make them both female. And most of the Red Tallon ones focus on the lupus one being smart and cool while the homid is a hapless dork.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 11-22-2019, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T18:37:07-08:00","id":1350362,"title":"","content":"First edition corebook stated, &quot;Most tribes originated out of a sept, and most septs first originated out of a pack. Thus the spirits of the tribes were once simply the spirits of a sept, and before that a pack.&quot;<br /> <br /> The canonical Central Park caern is perhaps an example of this, as we know the caern has two totems (Mera and Great White Mouse). The Great White Mouse was originally just the pack totem of the Marrow Eaters pack, and when they rescued/took over the caern in the 1930s, at some point their pack totem became a second caern totem.<br /> <br /> The original Garou did not have the Pact or any relations with spirits. The Garou had to navigate the spirit world, learn about their ways, and eventually discovered the laws of chiminage. With that knowledge, they began constructing the Pact with the spirits, and winning the favors of Totems, and learning Gifts and Rites. We can assume they started with pack totems, then caern totems, and finally tribal totems. Each probably required greater chiminage because they were getting the spirits to agree to adopt more and more children and agree to help Garou for a longer period of time. (The demands of spirit to assist a pack is much less than agreeing to assist all those future generations of Garou who will be part of a tribe).<br /> <br /> So it is simply a matter of Garou becoming experienced as they earned greater and greater privileges and responsibilities with the spirits.<br /> <br /> This probably took a few thousand years, and the different tribes were formed at different times. There is textual evidence that the Fianna was the first tribe, or must have been one of the first. Silver Fangs may have been second, but likely think they were the first. The Black Furies are also considered to be one of the older tribes. Star Gazers, Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers are some of the youngest tribes. Others are in between them.<br /> <br /> Incidentally,there is some evidence in early first edition material that the 13 tribes we know today (16 with the lost tribes) were only the surviving tribes, and that there were more at earlier points of time. First edition isn't consistent. There are statements of having only 15 tribes once (Croatan weren't invented yet, but soon would be). But there were also statements that implied there were many more, but they simply didn't survive. The Second Edition corebook actually tells us &quot;The Great White Mouse... predates the existence of the Bone Gnawers. He was once a minor totem of the Garou, but when the Bone Gnawers formed long ago, the followers of Mouse were slain by the Children of Rat.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T18:41:41-08:00","id":1350363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350232-when-and-why-did-the-garou-get-their-tribes?p=1350355#post1350355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in terms of prehistory, everything is supposed to be as vague as it needs to for things to be suitably mythic. Anything before @6000 BC in the WoD is pretty much an open canvas that can be whatever a gameline needs it to be. (And it's arguable that you may have had multiple realities happening at once, only to collapse in on itself at some point in the Bronze Age. This could possibly even include multiple realities in a single game line, resulting in conflicting myths and legends, or even memories in the case of the Mokole. The creationist nature of certain parts of Werewolf cosmology only add to it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually been compiling various quotes from canonical materials about what happened during the Stone Age as I find the lack of &quot;history&quot; in the game to be annoying (outside of singular &quot;events&quot; like the Impergium and War of Rage, the vast majority of a tribe's past is the Iron Age or younger). Since the Garou have an ancestral memory, this has bothered me.<br /> <br /> Now I'm thinking I should start a new thread and crowd source people to add things they know to it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T18:45:23-08:00","id":1350364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350232-when-and-why-did-the-garou-get-their-tribes?p=1350277#post1350277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A notable tid bit of all of this is that it's suggested in a few places that the reason why Wolf is no longer a totem of the Garou is that after his children turned their backs on him and each other to follow tribal totems, he departed into the deep umbra to never be heard from again.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my chronicles, I've always said that as Wolf is the father of all Garou, he can't show any favoritism to his children. So he can't be a totem to any of them. They already have their basic powers of shapechanging and such because of him. Same thing with Luna and Gaia. Although &quot;aspects&quot; of them can sometimes serve as totems which is why we have Old Wolf of the Woods, Winter Wolf, and Fenris as well as Phoebe and Danu.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T00:44:49-08:00","id":1350401,"title":"","content":"Ah yes, chiminige and pacts. That was another thing that Shattered Dreams mentioned to my surprise, that Garou didn't always have them. Again, I guess that it's something that developed slowly. Did they have them by the time of the War of Rage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T06:35:46-08:00","id":1350430,"title":"","content":"Shattered Dreams says the War of Rage began about 70,000 years ago, long before the Impergium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T06:59:11-08:00","id":1350434,"title":"","content":"I'll take that as a no then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T11:02:27-08:00","id":1350467,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, someone on rpg.net had a fairly indepth thread about stone age or precivilization Garou and Fera that was pretty interesting. I think some of it may have ended up as STV material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T21:57:58-08:00","id":1350580,"title":"","content":"What exactly is the &quot;War of Rage&quot; is something that should be taken with a grain of salt. The books make it sound like a formal war, but my personal opinion is that it is most like a construct of Garou historians in the same way that the Hundred Years War. (The Hundred Years War is something historians invented to link together several related, but distinct wars between the French and English. No one actually living at the time ever considered these separate events to be a single war.)<br /> <br /> In most published texts, the War of Rage is a distinct event that occurred after the Impergium ended.<br /> <br /> It is highly likely, IMHO, that the &quot;War of Rage&quot; combined many individual conflicts between the Garou and other Fera that have no actual connection to each other except for the fact that each conflict involves the Garou fighting other Fera. I believe the Garou, after the fact, combined various events and epic poems concerning these conflicts into one single narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T23:59:06-08:00","id":1350592,"title":"","content":"I thought the War of Rage was a long time before the Impergium ended,?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T02:37:01-08:00","id":1350613,"title":"","content":"The books that go into detail on it make it clear the Black Fox is right. There were a bunch of Wars of Rage over a long period of time, that get lumped together as one thing in Garou (and most Fera) history. One happened, supposedly, before the Garou and any of the other mammalian Fera even existed (hence no insect shifters!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T05:29:55-08:00","id":1350624,"title":"","content":"Ah yeah, the Anansi vs the insect-people?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T06:08:24-08:00","id":1350629,"title":"","content":"I only read Shattered Dreams. Do other books say different things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T10:02:18-08:00","id":1350660,"title":"","content":"Yes, other books say a lot of different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T16:27:57-08:00","id":1350924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350232-when-and-why-did-the-garou-get-their-tribes?p=1350363#post1350363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've actually been compiling various quotes from canonical materials about what happened during the Stone Age as I find the lack of &quot;history&quot; in the game to be annoying (outside of singular &quot;events&quot; like the Impergium and War of Rage, the vast majority of a tribe's past is the Iron Age or younger). Since the Garou have an ancestral memory, this has bothered me.<br /> <br /> Now I'm thinking I should start a new thread and crowd source people to add things they know to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you had a look at the Savage Age material on the vault for an alternate take?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T05:55:02-08:00","id":1351265,"title":"","content":"As others have said, it was hundreds, even thousands of little wars over eons. And I wouldn't be surprised if the reason the garou won had more to do with their kinfolk than the garou themselves. That is to say, the wolves out-competed the lions and so forth, which slowly reduced the territory in which other fera could breed, even if those fera won direct conflicts with the garou.<br /> <br /> And the whole story is pretty eurocentric. Did the garou win in Africa, for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T11:51:45-08:00","id":1351334,"title":"","content":"Well, the eurocentrism is some what justified in-universe as the majority of garou tribes are native to Eurasia and as such that's where they bothered to be active and the Wars of Rage and Impergium would have been most active.<br /> <br /> Africa didn't have many garou except for the Silent Striders in Egypt and the occasional tribal venturing into North African and the Fertile Crescent. Throughout the majority of Africa, it would have been the Ajaba and Simba Bastet who filled the roles of the potentially genocidal warmongers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T03:32:43-08:00","id":1351442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350232-when-and-why-did-the-garou-get-their-tribes?p=1351265#post1351265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the whole story is pretty eurocentric. Did the garou win in Africa, for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Silent Striders tribebook goes into more detail. Because the lack of wolf population of Africa, the War of Rage didn't affected that continent as much, but there were - if I remember correctly - clashes with the ruling Simbas.<br /> <br /> Asia was unaffected by the War of Rage, but they had the War of Shame when the local Gruhahl were destroyed.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Pure Lands&quot; were mostly affected by the Second War of Rage, breaking the Pure Tribes and wiping out the Xibalam.<br /> <br /> Australia were free of the War of Rage, but the native Bunyip was destroyed during the War of Tears.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T07:08:22-08:00","id":1351471,"title":"","content":"Who were the Xibalam?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T07:53:35-08:00","id":1351478,"title":"","content":"I think Lachdanan's mixing up the Camazotz with their Wyrm-corrupted variants, the Xibalan (introduced in W20 Book of the Wyrm). Prior to W20, the last Camazotz died in South America, but W20 shifted that to Australia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T00:59:48-08:00","id":1351610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350232-when-and-why-did-the-garou-get-their-tribes?p=1351478#post1351478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Lachdanan's mixing up the Camazotz with their Wyrm-corrupted variants, the Xibalan (introduced in W20 Book of the Wyrm). Prior to W20, the last Camazotz died in South America, but W20 shifted that to Australia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you are correct, my bad. And with n.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":562,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","user":"Lachdanan","date":". 11-29-2019, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}